VERDICT: REJECTED

The configured `Start application` workflow still executes `npx serve . -p 5000 --no-clipboard`, while the change only documents a different `npx --yes serve` command. On a fresh environment where `serve` is not already available, the configured command can wait for npm’s installation confirmation rather than start the site; the task’s workflow is therefore not reliably set up. The added `bash` module does not address this.

Security: none observed.

Next action: update the actual `.replit` workflow command to `npx --yes serve . -p 5000 --no-clipboard` (or add/pin `serve` as a project dependency), then verify the workflow reaches port 5000. Keep `replit.md` aligned with that final command.

